WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Why start here?

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:05.352
Because you can't make privilege
just-in-time until you can list it:

3
00:00:05.352 --> 00:00:09.065
who holds which role, at which
scope, standing or eligible,

4
00:00:09.065 --> 00:00:11.987
directly or through a
group, and in which tier.

5
00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:15.401
The admin center's list of
active assignments isn't enough.

6
00:00:15.401 --> 00:00:18.720
Under PIM almost every human
holder becomes eligible,

7
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.629
so a list of active assignments
shrinks as the project succeeds,

8
00:00:22.629 --> 00:00:25.875
and it stops being an inventory
just when you need one.

9
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:30.150
In this module you build the inventory
the rest of the path depends on:

10
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:34.725
one read of every privileged assignment,
a tier for every row, findings for

11
00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:39.500
standing privilege, and a manifest that
says which calls produced the files.
